From 6fbbaf8db39b62fa57cf788ec8427558cd3c8b16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Linghui Wu <linghui.wu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: shikra: Map WCSS firmware stream in EL2

When Shikra runs Linux directly at EL2, Gunyah does not configure the
IOMMU stream used by the WCSS firmware.  Without a wifi-firmware child
node ath10k assumes that TrustZone manages this stream and skips creating
the firmware IOMMU domain and identity mapping the WLAN MSA region.

The first firmware access to the WLAN MSA then causes a non-secure SMMU
global fault from stream ID 0x1a2, followed by a system NoC decode error
from qxm_wcss and a secure watchdog reset.

Describe the WCSS firmware stream in the EL2 overlay.  This makes ath10k
attach stream ID 0x1a2 to its firmware domain and map the WLAN MSA at its
physical address for firmware access.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Linghui Wu <linghui.wu@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/shikra-el2.dtso | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/shikra-el2.dtso b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/shikra-el2.dtso
index d2f3186bd47d..4d9e08d95d18 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/shikra-el2.dtso
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/shikra-el2.dtso
@@ -21,3 +21,9 @@
 		 <&apps_smmu 0x0366 0x0000>,
 		 <&apps_smmu 0x00e7 0x0000>;
 };
+
+&wifi {
+	wifi-firmware {
+		iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x01a2 0x0001>;
+	};
+};
